---
title: "divide_into_n (Sui Framework: coin)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_n: assert n > 0
    q_check_n --> q_abort_arg: n == 0
    q_abort_arg --> [*]: abort EInvalidArg
    q_check_n --> q_check_enough: n > 0
    q_check_enough --> q_abort_enough: n > self.value()
    q_abort_enough --> [*]: abort ENotEnough
    q_check_enough --> q_calc: n <= self.value()
    q_calc --> q_loop: split_amount = self.value() / n
    q_loop --> q_split: for i in 0..n-1
    q_split --> q_loop: self.split(split_amount, ctx)
    q_loop --> [*]: return vector of (n-1) coins

    note right of q_calc
        INV-001: each new coin has balance = floor(value/n)
        INV-002: remainder stays in self
        INV-003: sum of all coins (including self) = original value
        INV-004: rounding loss = value mod n stays in self
    end note
